# Editorial Studio

**AI Editorial Publishing Software** — Transform AI-generated manuscripts into professionally typeset, multi-page PDF publications.

## Overview

Editorial Studio is a complete, reusable publishing infrastructure that accepts manuscripts from AI agents and independently handles:

- **Editorial design & art direction** — AI art director plans the publication as a complete editorial product
- **Typography & layout** — Professional typesetting with Typst, supporting multiple design systems
- **Asset management** — Image generation, diagram creation, visual reference library
- **PDF rendering** — High-quality multi-page PDF output with proper pagination
- **Visual QA** — Automated page inspection, defect detection, and repair
- **Agent integration** — REST API, MCP server, and CLI for AI agent connectivity

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     Editorial Studio                        │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Ingestion  │──│ Intelligence│──│  Art Director       │  │
│  │  (MD/TXT/   │  │  (analysis, │  │  (plan, design,     │  │
│  │   DOCX/HTML)│  │   brief)    │  │   pagination)       │  │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └──────────┬──────────┘  │
│                                               │             │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────▼──────────┐  │
│  │    Asset    │──│   Renderer  │──│       QA Engine     │  │
│  │  (images,   │  │  (Typst)    │  │  (inspect, repair)  │  │
│  │   diagrams) │  └─────────────┘  └──────────┬──────────┘  │
│  └─────────────┘                              │             │
│                                               ▼             │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Publisher  │──│   Project   │──│  Agent Integration  │  │
│  │  (export,   │  │  Storage    │  │  (API, MCP, CLI)    │  │
│  │   bundle)   │  │  (SQLite)   │  └─────────────────────┘  │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘                            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
# Install Typst (required for PDF rendering)
brew install typst  # macOS
# or download from https://github.com/typst/typst/releases

# Install Editorial Studio
cd editorial_studio
pip install -e .
```

### CLI Usage

```bash
# Create a project and publish end-to-end
editorial-studio end-to-end manuscript.md \
  --brand educational \
  --title "My Course" \
  --author "Instructor" \
  --output course.pdf

# Or step by step:
editorial-studio create "My Project"
editorial-studio import --project <id> --file manuscript.md
editorial-studio configure-design --project <id> --brand educational
editorial-studio plan --project <id>
editorial-studio render --project <id>
editorial-studio export --project <id>
```

### API Server

```bash
# Start REST API server
editorial-studio api

# Or with uvicorn directly
uvicorn editorial_studio.api.server:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765
```

### MCP Server

```bash
# Run MCP server for AI agent integration
editorial-studio mcp
```

Configure in your MCP client (Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "editorial-studio": {
      "command": "editorial-studio",
      "args": ["mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

### Web Interface

```bash
# Start web management interface
editorial-studio web
# Open http://localhost:3000
```

## Supported Manuscript Formats

- **Markdown/MDX** — Full support including headings, lists, code blocks, tables, images
- **Plain Text** — Automatic structure detection
- **JSON** — Structured content blocks
- **HTML** — Semantic element extraction
- **DOCX** — Word document import with styles

## Design Systems

Built-in brand profiles:

| Profile | Use Case | Typography | Colors |
|---------|----------|------------|--------|
| `landnow` | Land investment publications | Source Serif 4 + Source Sans 3 | Navy + Brass |
| `institutional` | Financial reports | Source Serif 4 + Source Sans 3 | Navy |
| `educational` | Courses & workbooks | PT Serif + PT Sans | Teal |
| `scientific` | Technical guides | IBM Plex Serif + Sans | IBM Blue |
| `nature` | Travel & visual features | Lora + Cormorant | Violet |
| `minimalist` | Professional manuals | Inter + JetBrains Mono | Slate |

## Page Composition Families

- Cover, Title, Copyright, TOC
- Chapter/Part Openers
- Long-form Reading (single & two-column)
- Image-led & Full-width Image
- Diagrams, Tables, Comparison Tables
- Definitions, Sidebars, Pull Quotes
- Exercises, Worksheets, Quizzes
- Case Studies, Worked Examples
- Recaps, Summaries, Glossaries
- References, Appendices, Back Cover

## Agent Integration

### MCP Tools

| Tool | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `create_publication` | Create new project |
| `import_manuscript` | Import from file or content |
| `configure_design_system` | Set brand profile & overrides |
| `add_visual_reference` | Add Pinterest URL or image |
| `analyze_manuscript` | Analyze structure & content |
| `generate_editorial_plan` | Create full publication plan |
| `validate_editorial_plan` | Check plan for issues |
| `render_publication` | Generate PDF |
| `inspect_publication` | View QA results |
| `inspect_page` | Check specific page issues |
| `repair_page` | Fix layout defects |
| `regenerate_chapter` | Re-render single chapter |
| `get_job_status` | Check render progress |
| `get_qa_report` | Detailed QA report |
| `export_publication` | Get final PDF + source bundle |

### REST API

```
POST   /projects                    Create project
GET    /projects                    List projects
GET    /projects/{id}               Get project
POST   /projects/{id}/manuscript    Import manuscript
POST   /projects/{id}/design        Configure design
POST   /projects/{id}/references    Add visual reference
POST   /projects/{id}/plan          Generate editorial plan
POST   /projects/{id}/render        Render PDF
GET    /projects/{id}/status        Job status
GET    /projects/{id}/qa            QA report
GET    /projects/{id}/pages         Page previews
POST   /projects/{id}/repair        Repair page
POST   /projects/{id}/export        Export package
```

## Quality Assurance

Every render passes through automated QA:

1. **Page rendering** — Each PDF page rendered to high-DPI image
2. **Geometry checks** — Margins, safe areas, content bounds
3. **Content completeness** — No missing/duplicated blocks
4. **Typography** — Widows, orphans, line length, hyphenation
5. **Layout** — Overlap, clipping, balance, consistency
6. **Repair loop** — Auto-fix defects, re-render, re-inspect (max 3 attempts)

## Project Structure

```
editorial_studio/
├── core/                 # Models, database, config
├── content/              # Ingestion, intelligence
├── art_director/         # Editorial planning
├── design_system/        # Brand profiles, tokens
├── asset_engine/         # Images, diagrams, references
├── renderer/             # Typst PDF rendering
├── qa/                   # Visual QA & repair
├── export/               # Publishing & bundles
├── api/                  # FastAPI REST server
├── mcp/                  # Model Context Protocol server
├── cli/                  # Typer CLI
├── web/                  # Browser interface
├── assets/               # Fonts, templates
├── data/                 # SQLite, projects
└── tests/                # Test suite
```

## Configuration

`config.yaml` controls:

```yaml
storage:
  database_path: "data/editorial_studio.db"
  projects_root: "data/projects"

rendering:
  engine: "typst"
  typst_path: "typst"
  fonts_dir: "assets/fonts"

qa:
  max_repair_attempts: 3
  strict_layout: false

api:
  host: "127.0.0.1"
  port: 8765
```

Environment variables override config:
- `EDITORIAL_STUDIO_DB_PATH`
- `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `REPLICATE_API_KEY`

## Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
pytest editorial_studio/tests/ -v

# Run with coverage
pytest editorial_studio/tests/ --cov=editorial_studio

# Type checking
mypy editorial_studio/

# Linting
ruff editorial_studio/
```

## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- Typst 0.14+ (for PDF rendering)
- Poppler (for `pdftoppm` - PDF to image conversion in QA)
- Optional: Image generation APIs (OpenAI, Replicate, Stability)

